B.w4=new A.wX("Privacy Policy","Twins - Privacy Policy (template)\n\nWe collect:\n- Account info you provide (username, email).\n- Content you upload (videos, photos, captions, messages).\n- Basic usage data to keep the app working.\n\nLook-alike matching: to find people who look alike, we analyze faces in profile photos and in videos and photos posted on Twins, using Amazon Rekognition (Amazon Web Services). We store a face template (not a readable photo copy) linked to your account or post, and show matches only as a username and a blurred photo until revealed. This is biometric data: it is used only for matching, never sold, and deleted when you turn matching off, delete the post, or delete your account. You can switch this off any time in Settings > Privacy & Safety.\n\nWe do not sell your personal data. Messages between users are stored to enable the messaging feature.\n\nThis is a template - replace it with a real Privacy Policy, ideally reviewed by a lawyer, before publishing your app. It must be hosted at a public URL for Play Store / App Store submission, not just shown inside the app.\n",null)
B.w5=new A.wX("Terms of Service","Twins - Terms of Service (template)\n\nBy creating an account, you agree to:\n- Only post videos and photos you own or have permission to share, and only of people who are happy to appear in them.\n- Understand that look-alike matching analyzes the faces in profile photos, videos and photos posted on Twins. You can turn this off at any time in Settings > Privacy & Safety.\n- Not upload content that is illegal, harassing, hateful, sexually explicit involving minors, or otherwise violates applicable law.\n- Respect other users - no harassment, impersonation, or spam.\n- Understand that celebrity accounts require verification and a paid subscription.\n- Understand that your account may be suspended or removed for violating these terms.\n\nThis is a template - replace it with a real Terms of Service, ideally reviewed by a lawyer, before publishing your app.\n",null)
